# Asterix & Obelix: Babylon Mission (PPSA30490, Unity 6000.1.5f1 / IL2CPP)
# Reach GAMEPLAY: logo movies -> splash -> title menu -> intro cinematics -> world map -> a level.
#
# NOTE ON THE NAME. This is NOT the same game as scripts/asterix/reach-gameplay.pad, which drives
# Asterix & Obelix: Slap Them All! (PPSA08576, label game:asterix). That route does nothing here.
#
# Two phases, and the split is load-bearing:
#
#   Phase 1 (5-58 s) - Cross. Crosses the two publisher logo movies, the SPLASH scene and the
#     ADVENTURE / OPTIONS title menu. Cross is "Selection" throughout, including on the world map,
#     whose own footer reads "MAIN MENU (circle)  (cross) SELECTION".
#
#   Phase 2 (60 s+) - Triangle, with Cross interleaved 3 s later. Every cutscene frame draws a
#     "Skip" prompt bound to TRIANGLE, not Cross. A Cross-only mash therefore sits through the whole
#     intro: the first exploratory run watched Cinematic_A1_Part_1 -> A1_Part_2 -> A2 for 215 s and
#     never left them. Triangle is held 1.5 s so a hold-to-skip binding is covered as well.
#     What that run establishes is that Cross does not SKIP a cutscene, not that the cutscenes never
#     end on their own - it was bounded at 320 s and stopped 105 s into Cinematic_A2, so a longer
#     Cross-only run might reach gameplay by waiting. Triangle is what makes the path short and
#     bounded, which is what a route needs.
#
# Progression oracle, which is what this route was calibrated against - PROSPER_FILELOG=1 names the
# Unity scene files, and Media/levelNN is build-settings scene index NN (76 scenes, 76 files,
# verified by a byte-level scan of globalgamemanagers):
#
#   level0  videoLogos     level1  GlobalManager   level2  PauseManager   level5  MainMenu
#   level38 Cinematic_A1_Part_1    level39 Cinematic_A1_Part_2    level40 Cinematic_A2
#   level6  Loading        level4  Map             level3  PlatformerLogic
#   level22 World_3_10     level57 World_3_10_Level
#
# Measured on Linux/hardware Vulkan through tools/screenshot at PROSPER_RENDER_SCALE=1,
# PROSPER_RENDER_EVERY=1, native 1920x1080, with a private PROSPER_SAVE0 (see #2734 - the default
# save root is shared by every title on the box):
#
#   t~55 s   cinematics begin        t~125 s  cinematics done, world map ("Coastal Region")
#   t~165 s  level load              t~172 s  PlatformerLogic
#   t=180-240 s  the level's own title card ("ON THE ROAD TO UGARIT!") holds over the level
#   t=250 s -> unobstructed gameplay, unbroken to t=600 s (60/60 samples, pixel-distinct 58, guest
#   alive). Distinct colours per sample jump 2,170 -> 220,066 between t=240 s and t=250 s and then
#   hold at 214,981-220,066 for all 35 remaining samples: a snapshot guard should sample AFTER
#   t~250 s, or it will capture the title card instead of the level.
#
# Bound the run at >= 300 s. Reaching the map alone takes ~125 s on this host, and a short run ends
# inside the intro cinematics looking exactly like a title-menu stall.
#
# The Phase-2 mash deliberately continues through gameplay: Cross and Triangle are jump/attack there,
# which is harmless, and keeping it running is what makes the route tolerant of a slower host.
